# /setup-wiki — Initialize New Knowledge Space

When the user types `/setup-wiki`, begin the interactive workspace setup wizard.

---

## Shared Library

All shared components live in the workspace root's `.shared/` directory.
Use `bridge.ps1` to link shared components into the new Knowledge Space.

---

## Phase 1 — Gather Information (Interactive)

Ask the user these questions sequentially (use interactive_feedback or direct questions):

### Q1: Project Purpose
> "What is the main purpose of this wiki? Examples: research notes, tool comparison, learning journal, project documentation, personal knowledge base"

### Q2: Research Question (if applicable)
> "What central question are you investigating? (Leave blank if this is a general-purpose wiki)"

### Q3: Content Sources
> "Where will your content come from? Options:
> - Web clipping (browser extension)
> - Local documents (PDFs, DOCX, media files)
> - Manual notes
> - Code repositories
> - Academic papers
> - All of the above"

### Q4: Page Types Needed
> "Which page types do you need? (All will be available, but I'll configure the schema to prioritize yours):
> - entity (named things: people, tools, orgs)
> - concept (ideas, techniques, frameworks)
> - source (papers, articles, talks)
> - query (open questions)
> - comparison (side-by-side analysis)
> - synthesis (cross-cutting conclusions)
> - thesis (working hypotheses)
> - methodology (research methods)
> - finding (empirical results)"

### Q5: Naming Convention
> "How should files be named?
> - kebab-case (default: `my-page-name.md`)
> - Custom pattern?"

### Q6: Tags Strategy
> "What tag categories matter to you? Examples: topic, status, priority, source-type, year, confidence"

---

## Phase 2 — Generate Files

Based on answers, generate these files in order:

### 2.1 — Create Directory Structure

```
<space-name>/
├── purpose.md              ← Generated from Q1-Q2
├── schema.md               ← Generated from Q3-Q6
├── CLAUDE.md               ← Generated (space-specific guidance)
├── .space.json             ← Bridge metadata
├── raw/
│   ├── sources/            ← Immutable captured content
│   ├── extracts/           ← Extracted text (transcripts, OCR)
│   ├── transcripts/        ← Video/audio transcripts
│   └── assets/             ← Local images
├── wiki/
│   ├── index.md            ← Central catalog
│   ├── log.md              ← Activity log
│   ├── overview.md         ← Project summary
│   ├── entities/
│   ├── concepts/
│   ├── sources/
│   ├── queries/
│   ├── comparisons/
│   ├── synthesis/
│   ├── wiki-dashboard.base ← Obsidian metrics view
│   └── repo-tracker.base   ← Entity tracking view (if entity-heavy)
├── scripts/                ← JUNCTION → .shared/scripts
├── .obsidian/              ← Auto-generated vault config
├── .llm-wiki/
│   └── ingest-queue/       ← Pending ingest items
├── .cursor/
│   └── rules/              ← Hard links to .shared/cursor-rules + space-specific rules
├── .claude/
│   ├── commands/           ← JUNCTION → .shared/claude-commands
│   ├── skills/             ← JUNCTION → .shared/claude-skills
│   └── settings.json
└── graphify-out/           ← Created after first /graphify run
```

### 2.2 — Link Shared Components

Run the bridge script from the workspace root to set up all links:

```powershell
.\bridge.ps1 add-space "<space-name>"
```

This creates:
- Directory junctions for scripts/, .claude/skills/, .claude/commands/
- Hard links for shared cursor rules (.mdc files)
- A `.space.json` metadata file

### 2.3 — Generate `purpose.md`

Template (fill from Q1-Q2 answers):

```markdown
# Project Purpose — <Title from Q1>

## Research Question

> <From Q2, or generic statement based on Q1>

## Hypothesis / Working Thesis

> <Generated from Q1+Q2: what the user hopes to achieve>

## Background

<2-3 paragraphs explaining the context, generated from Q1+Q3>

## Sub-questions

<3-5 sub-questions derived from Q2>

## Scope

**In scope:**
<Generated from Q3 — what types of content will be captured>

**Out of scope:**
<Inferred boundaries>

## Methodology

<Generated from Q3+Q4 — how content flows through the system>

## Success Criteria

<Generated from Q1+Q2 — measurable outcomes>

## Current Status

> Initialized — workspace structure created, ready for first content capture.
```

### 2.4 — Generate `schema.md`

Template (fill from Q4-Q6 answers):

```markdown
# Wiki Schema — <Title>

## Page Types

| Type | Directory | Purpose |
|------|-----------|---------|
<Generated from Q4 — only include selected types>

## Naming Conventions

<From Q5>

## Frontmatter

<Standard YAML frontmatter spec, adapted for selected types>

## Index Format

`wiki/index.md` lists all pages grouped by type. Each entry:
- [[page-slug]] — one-line description

## Log Format

`wiki/log.md` records activity in reverse chronological order.

## Cross-referencing Rules

<Standard wikilink rules>

## Contradiction Handling

<Standard contradiction workflow>
```

### 2.5 — Generate `CLAUDE.md`

Generate a space-specific CLAUDE.md that:
- Describes the space's purpose and research question
- Includes the Auto-Ingest Pipeline section (shared workflow)
- Includes Skills Configuration section (obsidian-skills + graphify)
- Includes Integration with External Tools section
- Adapts Comparison & Recommendation Workflow if applicable

### 2.6 — Generate `wiki/index.md`, `wiki/log.md`, `wiki/overview.md`

Empty but properly structured starter files.

---

## Phase 3 — Install Dependencies (First-Time Only)

If these are not already installed globally:

### 3.1 — Graphify
```bash
pip install graphifyy
graphify cursor install
```

### 3.2 — Python Dependencies (for scripts)
```bash
pip install faster-whisper yt-dlp PyMuPDF python-docx openpyxl
```

### 3.3 — Defuddle (for web clipping)
```bash
npm install -g defuddle
```

### 3.4 — Obsidian Config
Create `.obsidian/` with recommended settings for wiki vault.

---

## Phase 4 — First Run Verification

Guide user through first content cycle:

1. **Test web clip**: Paste a URL, defuddle extracts, save to `raw/sources/`
2. **Test ingest**: Run `/ingest-pending` or manually trigger CLAUDE.md pipeline
3. **Test graphify**: Run `/graphify .` to verify `graphify-out/` is created
4. **Test sync**: Run `/graphify-to-wiki --dry-run` to verify detected pages
5. **Test dashboard**: Open `wiki/wiki-dashboard.base` in Obsidian

---

## Quick Reference Card

After setup, user can:

| Command | What it does |
|---------|-------------|
| `/extract-content` | Extract text from PDFs/docs/media in raw/ |
| `/extract-media` | Transcribe video/audio files |
| `/graphify .` | Build/rebuild knowledge graph |
| `/graphify-to-wiki` | Sync graph insights to wiki pages |
| `/ingest-pending` | Process queued raw sources into wiki |
| `/setup-wiki` | This wizard (re-run to reconfigure) |

| Script | What it does |
|--------|-------------|
| `python scripts/watch_ingest.py` | Watch for new files in raw/sources/ |
| `python scripts/extract_content.py` | Extract all file types |
| `python scripts/extract_media.py` | Extract video/audio only |

---

## Maintenance

- Run `/graphify . --update` after significant wiki changes
- Run `/graphify-to-wiki` periodically to sync new graph insights
- Check `wiki/wiki-dashboard.base` for connectivity metrics
- Review `wiki/log.md` for recent activity
- Run `.\bridge.ps1 verify` to check shared links are healthy
